# Homelab Build Log

A running log of my homelab build: Proxmox VE on an HP EliteDesk 800 G3 mini PC, with Tailscale for remote access.

## Goals

- Host websites
- Run my own VPN
- Set up a honeypot
- Run a network-wide ad-blocker
- Host a personal cloud server
- Add a larger storage unit later

## Hardware

| Item | Role |
|---|---|
| HP EliteDesk 800 G3 mini PC | Proxmox host (wiped, fresh install) |
| NETGEAR GS308 (8-port unmanaged switch) | Connects the lab devices |
| TP-Link router (second router) | Planned to sit in front of the lab for network isolation |
| Storage unit | Planned, not yet installed |

## Planned architecture

```
Internet -> Main router (home network)
                +-- Second TP-Link router (lab network, own subnet)
                        +-- GS308 switch -> Mini PC (Proxmox)
                                           (storage unit added later)
```

The switch is unmanaged, so it can't do VLANs. Putting the lab behind the second router gives real isolation, so a compromised honeypot can't reach personal devices.

### Planned services

| Goal | Plan |
|---|---|
| VPN | Tailscale (subnet router / exit node) |
| Ad-blocker | Pi-hole or AdGuard Home in an LXC container |
| Websites | LXC or Docker, exposed through a Cloudflare Tunnel (no open ports) |
| Cloud server | Nextcloud, with data on the future storage unit |
| Honeypot | Cowrie (or T-Pot) in an isolated VM |

Planned build order: Proxmox, Tailscale, Pi-hole, websites, Nextcloud, honeypot last.

